  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="417e-507f-a00a-6805" name="Republican Roman (Armies of Antiquity) - List Notes" publicationId="aab0-aa1e-0319-4ffe" hidden="false">
      <description>REPUBLICAN ROMAN ARMY LIST (Armies of Antiquity, pp.20-21), the citizen legions from c.400 BC to c.100 BC.
Characters: the army may have a General and an Army Battle Standard. Infantry at least half the points; Auxiliaries up to half; Special Units up to a quarter, and no more special units than the army has infantry and auxiliary units (not enforced).
Allies as special units from other lists (not built here: make a separate small roster): Numidians (any number of Barbarian Light Cavalry, Warriors but not Fanatic Warriors, and Skirmishers from the Barbarian list), Celts (Barbarian Noble Cavalry or Warriors, not Fanatic Warriors), Greeks (Peltasts and Skirmishers from the Ancient Greek list). All are subject to the Warband rules.
Manipular formation: a hastati, principes or triarii unit may swap places with another hastati or principes unit within 4" in its front arc (see the rule).

ARMY COMPOSITION (percentages by points):
  Infantry: at least 50%
  Auxiliaries: up to 50%
  Special Units: up to 25%</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
